 computed, the numerator for the ratio is end-of-period par, and denominator is tranche A’s balance *before* any principal repayment.\n\nSo let’s compute step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Period 1 start:\n\n- Par balance: $76,600,000  \n- Tranche A balance: $60,600,000  \n- Tranche B balance: $4,900,000\n\n#### Collections during period 1:\n\n- Interest: 9% × 76,600,000 =  \n  0.09 × 76,600,000 = **6,894,000**\n- Scheduled principal: $1,000,000  \n- Defaults: $6,500,000\n\nSo total cash available before any distribution:  \n= interest + scheduled principal = 6,894,000 + 1,000,000 = **7,894,000**\n\nNote: defaults reduce par balance but do *not* produce cash. So cash available is only interest + scheduled principal.\n\n#### End-of-period par balance:\n\n- Start par: 76,600,000  \n- Less scheduled principal: 1,000,000  \n- Less defaults: 6,500,000  \n= 76,600,000 − 1,000,000 − 6,500,000 = **69,100,000**\n\n#### Tranche A’s balance before OC diversion: still $60,600,000\n\nNow compute OC ratio before diversion:\n\n\\[\n\\text{OC ratio} = \\frac{\\text{end-of-period par}}{\\text{tranche A balance}} = \\frac{69,100,000}{60,600,000}\n\\]\n\nCompute:\n\n69,100,000 ÷ 60,600,000 ≈ ?\n\nLet’s compute:\n\n69.1 / 60.6 ≈\n\nDivide:  \n60.6 × 1.14 = 60.6 × 1 + 60.6 × 0.14 = 60.6 + 8.484 = 69.084  \nClose!  \n60.6 × 1.1403 ≈ 60.6 × 1.1403  \n= 60.6 × 1.14 + 60.6 × 0.0003 = 69.084 + 0.01818 = 69.10218\n\nSo 69.1 / 60.6 ≈ 1.140264...\n\nMore precisely:\n\n69,100,000 ÷ 60,600,000  \n= 691 / 606  \n= ?\n\nDivide 691 ÷ 606:\n\n606 × 1 = 606 → remainder 85  \n→ 850 ÷ 606 ≈ 1 → 606 × 1 = 606 → remainder 244  \n→ 2440 ÷ 606 ≈ 4 → 606 × 4 = 2424 → remainder 16  \n→ 160 ÷ 606 = 0.264...\n\nSo 1.140264...\n\nRounded to 2 decimal places: **1.14**\n\nBut wait — the question asks for the ratio as a **percentage**, and to give the number *without* the % sign.\n\nSo 1.14 as a percentage is 114%.\n\nWait — double-check wording:\n\n> \"what is the OC ratio at the end of period 1, before any diversion (end-of-period par as a percentage of tranche A's balance)?\"\n\nSo it’s:  \n(end-of-period par) ÷ (tranche A’s balance) × 100% → then drop the % sign.\n\nSo ratio is 69.1M / 60.6M ≈ 1.140264 → as percentage: 114.0264% → round to 2 decimals: **114.03**\n\n✅ Yes.\n\nLet’s compute precisely:\n\n69,100,000 ÷ 60,600,000 = ?\n\nDo exact division:\n\n69,100,000 / 60,600,000  \n= 691 / 606  \nSimplify? GCD of 691 and 606? 691 is prime? 691 ÷ 606 ≈ 1.140264026...\n\nNow multiply by 100:  \n= 114.02640264...\n\nRound to 2 decimal places: **114.03**\n\n✅\n\nSo final answer:  \n114.03\n\nOnly the number. No % sign.","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"exact_match","expected":"114.03","extract":"(-?\\d*\\.?\\d+)","nearMisses":[{"slip":"truncated","credit":0.5,"expected":"114.02"}]},"timing":{"wall_sec":16.583,"prompt_tokens":401,"generation_tokens":1582,"ttft_ms":317,"prefill_ms":317,"decode_ms":16254,"source":"client","cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"oc_waterfall_chain#2","prompt_name":"oc_waterfall_chain#2","family":"oc_waterfall","parent_item_id":"oc_waterfall_chain","turn":2,"prior_turn_passed":true,"output":"4444444","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"exact_match","expected":"5320000","extract":"(-?\\d[\\d,]*)(?:\\.0+(?!\\d))?"},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.405,"prompt_tokens":446,"generation_tokens":8,"ttft_ms":332,"prefill_ms":332,"decode_ms":61,"source":"client","cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"oc_waterfall_chain#3","prompt_name":"oc_waterfall_chain#3","family":"oc_waterfall","parent_item_id":"oc_waterfall_chain","turn":3,"prior_turn_passed":false,"output":"444444","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"exact_match","expected":"392000","extract":"(-?\\d[\\d,]*)(?:\\.0+(?!\\d))?"},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.406,"prompt_tokens":490,"generation_tokens":7,"ttft_ms":342,"prefill_ms":342,"decode_ms":51,"source":"client","cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"oc_waterfall_chain#4","prompt_name":"oc_waterfall_chain#